      "path": "tsc/internal/transformers/estransforms/definitions.go",
      "symbol": "GetESTransformer",
      "line": 24,
      "explanation": "Script-target dispatcher. It switches on options.GetEmitScriptTarget() (line 26) and, for ESNext, returns the composed esDecoratorAndClassFields(opts) (line 28); for ES2021-ES2026 it returns NewESNextTransformer (line 30) which embeds the same pair. The stage order is fixed by the package-level var esDecoratorAndClassFields = transformers.Chain(newESDecoratorTransformer, newClassFieldsTransformer) (line 9). transformers.Chain runs its components strictly left-to-right one source-file pass at a time (chain.go:20-22 construct components in order; chain.go:36-38 'Chains transforms in left-to-right order'), so the decorator stage always executes before the field/class-fields stage, and likewise NewESNextTransformer = Chain(newUsingDeclarationTransformer, esDecoratorAndClassFields) (line 10) keeps the using-declaration pass ahead of both. This dispatcher is the single entry point invoked from the emitter (emitter.go:164)."
