    {
      "path": "tsc/internal/transformers/estransforms/esdecorator.go",
      "symbol": "visitPropertyDeclaration",
      "line": 1574,
      "explanation": "Decorator-stage property visitor. It calls partialTransformClassElement (line 1600) which evaluates decorators and emits __esDecorate, creates memberInitializersName/memberExtraInitializersName helper vars, and registers the decoration statement via appendDecorationStatement. It then visits the initializer (line 1604) and wraps the field value in __runInitializers(this, _x_initializers, initializer) at line 1615 so decorator value-initializers produce the value. Earlier pending initializers are consumed and prepended into this field's value with injectPendingInitializers(ci, false, initializer) at line 1646, and this member's own extra initializers are queued afterward onto ci.pendingInstanceInitializers as __runInitializers(this, _x_extraInitializers) at lines 1648-1651. For a decorated auto-accessor it expands the single declaration into a backing field plus descriptor-forwarding getter/setter (lines 1658-1714), and caches a non-simple computed name so it is evaluated once (lines 1679-1694)."
