      "explanation": "Decorator-stage constructor visitor. It drains any remaining instance extra-initializers with initializerStatements := tx.prepareConstructor(tx.classInfoStack) (line 1194; prepareConstructor at 1122 emits __runInitializers(this, _instanceExtraInitializers) and clears the queue). It splits the standard prologue (line 1197), discovers the super-call location through transformers.FindSuperStatementIndexPath (line 1200, utilities.go:275), then places the drained initializer statements around that path with transformConstructorBodyWorker (line 1202). worker (line 1138) walks statements, recurses into a TryStatement containing super() (lines 1148-1169) using'initializerStatements, so the statements land immediately inside the try block right after super(); if no super path exists it appends them after the prologue (lines 1204-1206). The rebuilt body is given the original body's Loc/Loc metadata (lines 1210-1211)."
