      "explanation": "Field-stage constructor-body builder. It collects instance properties and private instance methods/accessors (lines 2504, 2512). Ordering is explicit: private-method branding is emitted first via addInstanceMethodStatements (line 2539, which calls WeakSet.add through createPrivateInstanceMethodInitializer at 2836-2851) with the comment 'private methods can be called in property initializers, they should execute first'; then parameter properties are separated from ordinary fields using the original-node metadata MostOriginal/IsParameterPropertyDeclaration (lines 2542-2547) and appended before non-parameter fields (lines 2548-2549). The resulting initializerStatements are placed relative to the discovered super call by transformConstructorBodyWorker (line 2569), which itself re-detects parameter-property statements via MostOriginal (lines 2484-2492) and preserves try-block nesting; a synthetic super(...arguments) is generated for a derived class with no constructor (lines 2586-2604). Variable environment statements are merged last (line 2608)."
